---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Glyph from '../components/Glyph.astro';
import SignalKey from '../components/SignalKey.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SOCIAL } from '../consts';

// The bio. Dad first, then what I do, then the ordinary human parts. The lede
// paragraph carries the premise; the rest is normal body text so the block has
// hierarchy instead of one flat wall. Every fact is Mel's own or sourced; no
// invented anecdotes, no CV stack, no em-dashes.
---

<BaseLayout title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Who The Token Dad is.">
  <div class="shell page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <p class="post-lede">I forget things, so I build machines that don't.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="shell column stack">
    <p class="lede">
      I'm Mel, a new dad in Mexico City. Most of what I build starts at home: the
      calendar, the messages, the hundred small handoffs that used to live in my
      head and leak out of it. I hand them to agents, and I publish what it costs
      to run them. Real bills, per model, with the method attached so you can
      check my work. I get numbers wrong sometimes; when I do, the correction
      goes up here too.
    </p>

    <p>
      The rest of the time I'm a founder. I started Pokta Labs, a frontier lab
      accelerating healthcare and education, and I run Frutero Club, a tech
      community that works as a talent accelerator for builders who want to level
      up professionally. The job has always been the same one: take a
      complicated system and make it usable by someone who didn't build it. The
      agents I run at home are that same discipline; they just show up wearing
      sweatpants.
    </p>

    <p>
      Off the clock I'm about as ordinary as they come. Cancún raised me,
      Monterrey put me through school, and Mexico City has been home since 2013.
      I support Club América, Manchester United, and the Dallas Cowboys, which is
      a lifelong commitment to caring far too much about games I'll never play
      in. I play tennis and football most weeks, and I'll happily lose an evening
      to history, geopolitics, sci-fi, fantasy, a good game, or music.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm also the three-time champion of the International Super Smash Brothers
      Big Walrus Invitational, title successfully defended last week at the sixth
      edition. It is exactly as prestigious as it sounds.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell column stack">
    <h2 class="section-title">The signs</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Every post carries one or two marks that say what kind of post it is,
      before you read a word of it. Six shapes, one drawing rule, one colour
      each.
    </p>
    <SignalKey variant="list" />
    <p class="meta">
      Red belongs to Correction and to nothing else, so a published number that
      changed is the loudest thing on the site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell column stack stack-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Elsewhere</h2>
    <div class="marks marks--labelled">
      <a class="quiet-link" href={SOCIAL.x} rel="me noopener">
        <span>X</span>
      </a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href={SOCIAL.github} rel="me noopener">
        <span>GitHub</span>
      </a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href={SOCIAL.linkedin} rel="me noopener">
        <span>LinkedIn</span>
      </a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href={SOCIAL.instagram} rel="me noopener">
        <span>Instagram</span>
      </a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href="/rss.xml">
        <Glyph name="feed" size={18} />
        <span>RSS</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
